A.exv=new B.br(10,3,"Shopping and consumer choices","\uc1fc\ud551\uacfc \uc18c\ube44 \uc0dd\ud65c","Explain a contrast between a condition and a result, and read a sample store policy carefully.","-\uc544/\uc5b4\ub3c4","Add \uc544/\uc5b4\ub3c4 to a verb or adjective to express even if or although: \ube44\uc2f8\ub3c4, even if it is expensive; \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud574\ub3c4, even if one uses it. The second clause holds despite the first condition. Compare \ube44\uc2f8\uc11c \uc548 \uc0ac\uc694, I do not buy it because it is expensive, with \ube44\uc2f8\ub3c4 \uc0ac\uc694, I buy it even though it is expensive. In -\uc544/\uc5b4\ub3c4 \ub3fc\uc694, the complete phrase asks or grants permission instead.","\uac00\uaca9\uc774 \uc2f8\ub3c4 \ud488\uc9c8\uacfc \uad50\ud658 \uc870\uac74\uc744 \ud655\uc778\ud574\uc694.","Even if the price is low, I check the quality and exchange conditions.",A.a7,A.a7,A.aV,A.k6Y,A.k0X,A.jUl)
