A.m8i=new B.fr([1,"The late equipment check unexpectedly delayed the event. -\ub294 \ubc14\ub78c\uc5d0 marks the cause; the morning start was only a plan.",2,"The materials were sent yesterday, but the list will be checked again tomorrow. -\ub824\uace0 \ud55c\ub2e4 expresses that intention.",3,"The speaker thought the rain had stopped, but it had only weakened briefly; it was still raining.",4,"A small number of applicants does not, by itself, prove that the program has little effect.",5,"The notice concerns enrollment rules and dates. Wednesday has three places, but only first-time applicants can take them.",6,"The notice explains how to borrow and return umbrellas. The key pickup location depends on the day; the umbrella always goes back to the first-floor box.",7,"Only the lakeside path closes at 7 p.m. until Friday. The park and other paths keep their usual hours.",8,"The notice gives inspection and replacement hours. Inspection is free; replacement parts cost money and are unavailable on Saturday morning.",9,"June 15 is the original-file deadline for selected applicants, before the June 20 winners announcement. June 10 is the initial entry deadline.",10,"February had exactly 100 more library visitors than January. The groups may overlap, so 450 and 180 cannot simply be added as distinct people.",11,"72 out of 90 respondents is 80% of survey respondents. It does not establish the satisfaction rate of all 200 people.",12,"Minji visited the station but did not meet her friend there. The ticket was handed over and received in separate steps at the exhibition area.",13,"The district first published the average (\ub098). Some residents reacted (\ub2e4); others then requested rainy-day figures after hearing that reaction (\uac00).",14,"Reserved seats sold out (\ub098). Absences then freed seats (\uac00), which were offered to people waiting on site (\ub2e4).",15,"Automatic figures appear first (\ub098). \uadf8\ub7fc\uc5d0\ub3c4 introduces their limitation (\uac00); \uadf8\ub798\uc11c leads to an additional field check (\ub2e4).",16,"A total trip count does not show direction or which groups use a stop. Boardings and exits need separate measurement.",17,"More received applications do not prove that processing is easier. Completion time and duplicate paperwork also matter.",18,"The same plant variety produced different results at different sites. Consider soil conditions before blaming the variety.",19,"Connection problems caused some late uploads; \uadf8 \ub54c\ubb38\uc5d0 links that problem to the school\u2019s response.",20,"Submission time alone is insufficient to judge a student\u2019s effort. The school also checks connection issues without waiving the assignment.",21,"The staff member was surprised that the resident who cleaned weekly, rather than a staff member, contributed the most photographs.",22,"That resident contributed many photographs. Pictures from another village are reserved for the next exhibition after their source is checked.",23,"The narrator feels sorry for worrying their mother but relieved after hearing her voice.",24,"The mother had sent the small lamp before the call; the narrator only contacted her in the evening.",25,"The trial is extended by one month. A decision on permanent operation is due at the end of the year.",26,"Visitors recovered, but accommodation bookings remained weak. The headline describes two different measures.",27,"Only the last bus leaves 30 minutes later; the first bus keeps its original time.",28,"Repeated video plays may signal careful study or confusion. Plays alone do not measure learning outcomes.",29,"Ordinary alerts and evacuation alerts involve different levels of risk. Both the frequency and the content should be adjusted.",30,"A ramp alone is insufficient when the same entrance still has a raised threshold and a heavy door.",31,"More gate entries do not necessarily mean more distinct visitors: one person can pass through more than once.",32,"The experience room, not the exhibition room, is free. Saturday visits require online booking; group bookings are closed on Monday.",33,"Water use fell 20% overall, while production fell 30%. That does not show a 20% decrease for each product.",34,"Both sites planted the same number of trees and became cooler, but shade increased by different amounts. Shade alone does not explain everything.",35,"Choice \u2461 may describe a detail, but the broader point separates book sales from people\u2019s ability to attend the reading club.",36,"Choice \u2460 reports an event. The main point is that meeting attendance alone does not measure overall participation.",37,"Distinguish litter left by visitors from litter blown in from the harbor, then consider collection times. The other options misassign the cause.",38,"More people come to take photos, while residents face slippery steps after rain. The passage contrasts those two outcomes.",39,"\uadf8\uac00 \ubc29\uae08 \ub0b4\ub9b0 \ud310\ub2e8 refers to the manager\u2019s just-made inference that the number of users doubled, so insert the sentence after \u3261.",40,"The sentence about workers missing from the survey belongs after they are introduced and before the weekend class is reopened.",41,"\uadf8 \uc0dd\uac01 points to the craftsperson\u2019s belief that keeping the same time was enough; insert it after that belief and before the change in measurement.",42,"The narrator initially overwatered a plant after misreading drooping leaves. Reading the care notes and seeing the plant recover brought relief.",43,"On the second occasion, the narrator read the instructions before watering. The mistaken assumption happened the first time.",44,"\ub2e4\ub9cc adds a qualification: on-time departure still matters to people waiting at the terminal, although it does not measure waits midway.",45,"Keep the departure measure but add real arrival times at each stop. The slowest section has yet to be identified.",46,"Closing soon after rent support ends does not prove every business failed for the same reason; the writer favors examining customers and survival.",47,"The district examined the customers of shops that survived after support ended; it did not assume every failure was caused by the end of rent aid.",48,"The author rejects conclusions based only on the next day\u2019s total or on immediate bridge expansion. Peak-hour and nearby-path data are needed.",49,"A surge just after the festival can produce a long wait even when daily totals look similar. The one-hour peak matters.",50,"The team chose further investigation, not bridge expansion. Traffic normalized the next day; the long queue came after the festival, and nearby paths still need checking."],t.TM)
